(22, '1672515987.jpg', 'WHAT GOD IS SAYING ABOUT 2023', '', '', 'Pastor Simon Mungwa', '2031-12-22 07:16:53', '2023-10-31 05:24:31', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong></strong>Beloved of God,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As we begin a new year, it is my joy to share with you what the good Lord has put on my heart to tell His people, a word in season to inspire and propel us into what He has in store for the year 2023. This is the joy we have to walk with the Holy Spirit, that we can know the future. Jesus assured us, &ldquo;When He, the Spirit of truth, has come, He will guide you into all truth; for He will not speak on His own authority, but whatever He hears He will speak; and He will tell you things to come&rdquo; (John 16:13).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Lord spoke to my heart saying, <strong>2023 IS A GREAT YEAR!</strong> Now, that is something to note. It is one thing to say a year is going to be great, but it is all together something else when the Lord Himself makes that announcement. The Lord gave more details to what will make it a great year, such things I am glad to share with you today. It is a year of a seven-fold blessing.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR OF BIRTHINGS</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It will be a year of birthings because the Lord will be bringing forth new things in our lives. These might be new career opportunities, new relationships, new business ideas, new ministry assignments, and of course birth of divinely appointed kids. He will launch us into new things and experiences. It is a year of bringing forth new things, such as take us steps further into God&rsquo;s plans for our lives. Even as it is written, <em>&ldquo;Do not remember the former things, nor consider the things of old. <u>Behold, I will do a new thing</u>, now it shall spring forth; Shall you not know it?&rdquo; (Isaiah 43:18-19).</em></p>\r\n<ol start=\"2\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR OF DIVINE SUPPLIES</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this new year, God shall bring us supernatural supplies to enable us fulfill His assignments to us. Just as it is written, <em>&ldquo;God shall supply all your need according to His riches in glory by Christ Jesus&rdquo; (Philippians 4:19).</em> Note that He does not say He will supply your needs according to your bank account. He will do so according to the boundless riches of Christ. Just as Paul wrote, <em>&ldquo;God is able to make all grace abound toward you, that you, always having all sufficiency in all things, may have an abundance for every good work&rdquo; (2 Corinthians 9:8)</em>. God is able to give us all sufficiency, nothing lacking, nothing missing. So this year we can say with even greater confidence, <em>&ldquo;The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not be in want&rdquo; (Psalm 23:1).</em></p>\r\n<ol start=\"3\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR OF PRESERVATION</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Despite the chaos in the world and the diseases that seem to multiply, God will preserve us from all forms of danger and harm, He will keep us from the evil one. He gave us this word, <em>&ldquo;No weapon formed against you shall prosper, and every tongue which rises against you in judgment you shall condemn. This is the heritage of the servants of the Lord, and their righteousness is from Me&rdquo;</em> (Isaiah 54:17). You can see Psalm 91:3-7 for additional emphasis.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"4\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR OF RESTORATION</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God is concerned about the things we have lost and the things we have had reasons to mourn over in the past. Even as He tells us to forget the former things, this year, He will be restoring somethings in our lives, even the years we might have considered to have been wasted. It is a year of restoration in our resources, relationships, and opportunities. And it will be for the better. Do not mourn any more over the past, look to the restoration of the Lord. He assures us, <em>&ldquo;I will restore to you the years that the swarming locust has eaten&rdquo; (Joel 2:25).</em></p>\r\n<ol start=\"5\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR WITH OPEN ACCESS WAYS</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Access to the right people in certain spheres is all you need for a shift in your life. Even so access into your life by certain people is all you need, that they may bring to you the blessings the Lord has given them for your life. That is why this year, the Lord himself is ensuring an open access in our lives for a two-way traffic. Free access to places of great treasures, even as people with treasures find access to us. Just as it is written, <em><u>&ldquo;Your gates will be open continually; They will not be closed day or night</u>, So that people may bring you the wealth of the nations, with their kings led in procession&rdquo; (Isaiah 60:11).</em> Yes, the Lord is keeping open access ways that will make for great connections and the flow of resources for His glory. He also declares, <em>&ldquo;Behold, <u>I set before you an open door</u>, which no man can shut&rdquo; (Revelation 3:8).</em></p>\r\n<ol start=\"6\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR OF STRATEGIC POSITIONING</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Positioning is everything, being at the right place at the right time. Jesus said, <em>&ldquo;No one lights a lamp and then puts it under a basket. Instead, a lamp is placed on a stand, where it gives light to everyone in the house&rdquo; (Matthew 5:15).</em> This year the Lord will be positioning us in strategic places for the revelation of His glory. This might sometimes come with seeming discomfort in the transition. For Joseph to be strategically positioned, he was imprisoned. And there in prison, he met the person who recommended him to the king. In the end, he was greatly exalted. Someone might lose a job for the better. If ever such should happen, rejoice in the shift God has prepared. <u>For it will be from glory to glory only</u>.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"7\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>A YEAR OF DIVINE ACCELERATION</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Acceleration is when we continually gain speed. It does not just mean going fast, it means the fastness is increasing with time. And this year we are gaining speed by the spirit of God. When people think we were moving fast, they will be surprised by how much faster we can go. When people think we are doing big things, they will be surprised by what bigger things we can do, and how much faster we can get them done. Divine acceleration is when God himself has His leg on the accelerating pedal of the car. You can do nothing about it but sit back, relax and key to the flow. Ahab the King had the fastest horses and Chariots. But when the Spirit of God took over Elijah, he ran on foot, faster than the horses to get ahead of the king ( See 1 Kings 18: 41- 46). &nbsp;This is what we are looking at, such supernatural speed in some things that you could hardly imagine possible, speed that will continue to increase so that we go faster, and faster as the year unfolds. Yes, the Lord is accelerating things in our lives this new year.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>YOUR RESPONSIBILITY IS SIMPLE</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What a year to look forward to! Now this does not mean it is a year free of challenges. However, the challenges we will face will only come as steppingstones to raise us higher. God will cause all things to work for our good, no matter what comes our way. And at the end of the next year, we will indeed look back to testify: &ldquo;It was a great year!!&rdquo;.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The call for you is to continue in the word of God, meditating therein and watching to do as the Lord instructs you by His word and by His Spirit. For it is in His paths that these blessings are guaranteed to us. Make commitments more than ever before to seek the kingdom of God and its righteousness above all, give to missions as the Lord enables and leads you, and make yourself available for the service of the Lord wherever He calls you. And you will see these blessings manifest fully in your life.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is my sincere prayer for you, that you will find grace to abide in the Lord and walk in His paths as He makes manifest, all these great blessings in your life through 2023 and beyond. I look forward to reading from you, as God confirms His word in your life.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With love,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pastor Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Email:&nbsp;</strong>PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</p>', '', '', 'news', '0', '1', '2022-12-31', '0000-00-00'),
(23, '1675980860.jpg', 'THE POSSIBILITIES ARE ENDLESS', '', '', 'Pastor Simon Mungwa', '2009-02-23 10:09:44', '2023-02-10 06:57:44', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beloved of God,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As we take on this month of February, it is my joy to reach you with a prophetic word in season from the Lord. And as you will see from the caption, it is a season of endless possibilities. That is God speaking to us, assuring us that this season, anything is possible. I therefore write to share with you by the Spirit of God, the response expected of us as we unleash our faith for the realization of that which would normally have been thought impossible.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I like to start by bringing you to the experience of the prophet Ezekiel. I will recommend you read the full story for yourself from Ezekiel 37:1-10 to have a full picture. The prophet recounts his experience of how the Lord brought him by the Spirit to a valley full of dry bones that had been disjointed from each other. Such a lifeless sight to behold. Then the Lord asked him: &ldquo;Son of man, can these bones live?&rdquo; And Ezekiel answered, &ldquo;Sovereign Lord, you alone know.&rdquo;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Lord exposed Ezekiel to such a sight that was short of any imaginable outcome of life. It was such a hopeless situation; the prophet could not answer if such bones could live again. The Lord had hoped that Ezekiel would know it was possible. It was a similar thing with Sarah. Together with the Husband Abraham, they had been trusting the Lord for a child. Finally, the appointed time came, and the Lord visited the couple. Then the Lord spoke to Abraham concerning the birth of a child. But Sarah had a different response. She saw no possibilities. The bible tells us: <em>&ldquo;So she laughed silently to herself and said, &lsquo;How could a worn-out woman like me enjoy such pleasure, especially when my master&mdash;my husband&mdash;is also so old?&rsquo; Then the LORD said to Abraham, &lsquo;Why did Sarah laugh? Why did she say, Can an old woman like me have a baby?&rsquo; <strong>Is anything too hard for the LORD? </strong>I will return about this time next year, and Sarah will have a son.&rsquo;&rdquo; (Genesis 18:12-14)</em></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Just like it was for Sarah, the Lord had to affirm to Ezekiel in the valley of dry bones that there was possibility of life from those dry bones. And it is not uncommon that we find ourselves in the face of such situations or adversities in our lives concerning our health, finances, career, ministry, and just diverse expectations, where it seems there are no possibilities. The Lord might have put in your heart a very big vision, even as He has put in my heart, such great things it would take miracles to accomplish. There is no need to wonder if it is possible. The Lord says to us this season, &ldquo;The possibilities are endless&rdquo;.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Back to Ezekiel&rsquo;s experience, we can already see what happens finally and the response God is requesting of us this season. After the Lord showed Him the dry bones, He went on to tell the servant: <em>&ldquo;Prophesy to these bones, and say to them, &lsquo;O dry bones, hear the word of the Lord! Thus says the Lord God to these bones: &ldquo;Surely I will cause breath to enter into you, and you shall live. I will put sinews on you and bring flesh upon you, cover you with skin and put breath in you; and you shall live. Then you shall know that I am the Lord.&rdquo; (Ezekiel 37:4-6).</em></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What a word! The possibilities are indeed endless. However, that was not going to happen without the involvement of Ezekiel. It was going to be a work of partnership with God. So the Lord showed Ezekiel what part He had to play. He was going to prophesy and declare the word of the Lord to the bones. And the prophet recounts: <em>&ldquo;So I prophesied as I was commanded; and as I prophesied, there was a noise, and suddenly a rattling; and the bones came together, bone to bone. Indeed, as I looked, the sinews and the flesh came upon them, and the skin covered them over; <u>but there was no breath in them</u>&rdquo;.</em> Something happened when He prophesied as commanded. The power of God was brought on the scene to accomplish that which was spoken. However, the miracle was not yet complete. At least, it had gone from dried scattered bones to a pile of corpses. Even so, never think nothing is happening. When you start speaking, things start shifting. But you must not stop until you see the full manifestation.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Lord was not going to do it all alone. So He gave the prophet the next instruction. &ldquo;Speak a prophetic message to the winds, son of man. Speak a prophetic message and say, &lsquo;This is what the Sovereign Lord says: Come, O breath, from the four winds! Breathe into these dead bodies so they may live again.&rsquo;&rdquo; So I spoke the message as he commanded me, and breath came into their bodies. They all came to life and stood up on their feet&mdash;a great army.&rdquo; (Ezekiel 37:9-10).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This brings us to the simple instructions for you. It all sums up in this: UNLEASH YOUR FAITH. This is the only response God expects of you. That&rsquo;s a word by the Spirit. To unleash means to release in a violent way. In this case, it means, set no limits on your faith. Go all out with it, for that is the only limiting thing. If your faith says yes to it, God won&rsquo;t say no! And you will unleash your faith by these three things simply.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>BELIEVE GOD&rsquo;S WORD</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Whatever God has said concerning you or a situation, is for you to accept it to be so. That is the meaning of believing. And because you believe, it is as good as done. Don&rsquo;t entertain any arguments of why it is not possible or what makes it illogical. It is not a season to debate with the word, but to believe. Just as Jesus declared: <strong><em>If you can believe, all things are possible to him who believes.&rdquo; (Mark 9:23).</em></strong> Also, Luke 1:45 assures us, \"Blessed&nbsp;<i>is</i>&nbsp;she who&nbsp;<span face=\"system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu, Cantarell, Noto Sans, sans-serif, Arial\" style=\"font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Noto Sans\', sans-serif, Arial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 6.875px;\">b</span></span>elieved, for there will be a fulfillment of those things which were told her from the Lord.&rdquo; Jesus once asked Martha, \"<span class=\"woj\">Did I not say to you that if you would believe you would</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span class=\"woj\">see the glory of God?&rdquo; And when Jairus heard news the daughter was dead and there was no longer any need to trouble the master, Jesus ignored the crowd and the news, turned around and said to the man, <strong>\"Only believe\" (Mark 5:36).&nbsp;</strong>Believe therefore to see the wonders of God in any given situation this season. Nothing is impossible when you believe.</span></p>\r\n<ol start=\"2\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>SPEAK THE WORD</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What is it you are expecting to see happen? You will have to speak it forth. Just like Ezekiel said, &ldquo;As I began to prophesy as commanded, there was a noise, and suddenly a rattling; and the bones came together, bone to bone.&rdquo; Something moves when you speak. God is looking to honor the words of your lips this season.&nbsp; Just as it is written: <strong><em>You will also declare a thing, And it will be established for you; So light will shine on your ways (Job 22:8)</em></strong>. Jesus also said: <strong><em>For assuredly, I say to you, whoever says to this mountain, &lsquo;Be removed and be cast into the sea,&rsquo; and does not doubt in his heart, but believes that those things he says will be done, he will have whatever he says (Mark 11:23)</em></strong>.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"3\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>TAKE NECESSARY ACTION</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Referring to the ability of faith to make for unimagined possibilities, the author of Hebrews wrote: <em>&ldquo;Time would fail me to tell of Gideon and Barak and Samson and Jephthah, also of David and Samuel and the prophets: <strong><u>who through faith</u></strong> subdued kingdoms, worked righteousness, obtained promises, stopped the mouths of lions, quenched the violence of fire, escaped the edge of the sword, out of weakness were made strong, became valiant in battle, turned to flight the armies of the aliens&rdquo; (Hebrews 11:32-34). </em>Sometimes your faith needs more than declarations. It needs action. While you speak, act. Take bold, courageous, and audacious steps this season and you will be surprised what a wonder God will make out of your seeming small steps of faith (For further study, read 2 Kings 7. Read the full chapter but pay close attention to verses 3 through 8).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">And it is indeed my prayer that this season and beyond will be for you a season of endless possibilities. That God will show Himself strong in your life and cause you to dance for the impossibilities made possible.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I will be glad to hear from you, how the word of God is impacting your life and empowering you for destiny. You can also partner with us as we bring the word of God to the nations at great cost. Send me a personal email at <a href=\"mailto:pastorsimon@lgmissions.org\">pastorsimon@lgmissions.org</a>.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God bless you</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pastor Simon Mungwa</strong></p>', '', '', 'news', '0', '1', '2023-02-09', '2023-02-09'),
(24, '1705500827.jpg', 'THE YEAR OF THE ENLIGHTENED CHURCH', '', '', 'Pastor Simon Mungwa', '2006-01-24 12:16:27', '2024-01-17 02:13:47', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beloved of God,&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I use this opportunity to wish you a happy new year and pray it will be for you another year that takes you further into God\'s plan for your life. As much as we celebrate another calendar year starting, it is much more a blessing to step into it, recognizing what God has purposed for us as His people. God always sends us His word ahead of His actions. As it is written: &ldquo;Surely the Sovereign LORD does nothing without revealing his plan to his servants the prophets&rdquo; (Amos 3:7). God gives us His word as His servants to communicate to His people, so that together, we can be aligned with His plans and be in step with Him. Moreover, by receiving the message the Lord is giving us, we receive the blessings that come with it. For God&rsquo;s word carries with it, the power and grace to make the word a reality in a life.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now, it may happen that many different persons receive different messages. The multiple messages do not invalidate the authenticity of these communications. This happens because God has a message for a people, as He has called them and positioned them in a given battalion of His great army, which is the Church of Christ. We should also be open to such messages and evaluate them by the Spirit of God to know what the Lord is saying to His people. Even as it is written: &ldquo;Do not scoff at prophecies, but test everything that is said. Hold on to what is good&rdquo; (1 Thessalonians 5:20-21).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We have such a word given to me from the Lord for you this season, a word of what He has purposed for us this year as His Children. The Lord says it shall be <strong>&ldquo;The year of the enlightened Church.&rdquo; For He will be illuminating the Church so she can know her true identity and empowering her to take her rightful place in the world.</strong> And this is also true for you as an individual: God will be enlightening you to know who you are in Christ Jesus, revealing to you your purpose in more details and empowering you to take your place like that city upon the hill that cannot be hidden (See Ephesians 1:18 and Matthew 5:14).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GOD IS ILLUMINATING HIS PEOPLE</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Illumination is insight, illumination is revelational truth, when God causes you to receive truth from His word or from His spirit that is relevant for the times. This is the illumination God wants to bring to you this year. That more than ever before, you will know who you are in Christ, recognize what God has called you to do, know the things He has placed at your disposal for the fulfilment, see His will for you and walk in it. That is what we are looking at &ndash; a year that brings you such information you need to be set at the center of God&rsquo;s will for your life. While God will be accomplishing this in the the universal church as a whole, He will also be accomplishing same in your life as an individual.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GOD IS EMPOWERING THE CHURCH</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To empower means to give ability. And this is something God is accomplishing with His universal church and in your life as an individual. This means empowerment by the Spirit, giving you supernatural ability to accomplish what you might otherwise have never accomplished. Empowerment also will be by placement, the Lord strategically giving us platforms that enable us shine His light and bring glory to His name. Empowerment also means making available the resources. As we well know, resources could be the limiting factor often. But this year, God is bringing to us the resources we need to fulfill His call, He is empowering us with substance. As it is written: And God is able to make all grace [every favor and earthly blessing] come in abundance to you, so that you may always [under all circumstances, regardless of the need] have complete sufficiency in everything [being completely self-sufficient in Him], and have an abundance for every good work and act of charity. (2 Corinthians 9:8 Amplified).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>YOUR RESPONSIBILITY</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With this prophetic word for the year, God calls us to a few responsibilities.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Give attention to His word:</strong> The word of God is light and by it, He brings to us illumination. Your Daily Light devotional is also a blessing to us, providing an avenue by which we can continually be nourished in God&rsquo;s word. If God will bring you illumination, you will have to give Him your attention. &ldquo;My son, give attention to my words; incline your ear to my sayings. For they are life to those who find them, and health to all their flesh&rdquo; (See Proverbs 4:20-22).</li>\r\n<li><strong>Recognize the person of the Holy Spirit</strong>: The word of God might inform us of things that were written, but the Holy Spirit is the one who brings to us such knowledge concerning things that are not written in the word. For example, you might be needing directions regarding your job, or other investment opportunities. The Holy Spirit is the one who has information to lead you. It is one reason He came. This year do well to recognize His person and learn to listen to Him. As Jesus promised: &ldquo;When the Spirit of truth comes, He will guide you into all the truth. For He will not speak on His own, but He will speak whatever He hears. He will also declare to you what is to come&rdquo; (John 16:13).</li>\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>Walk by faith: </strong>There has never been a greater call to walk by faith. As the age draws to a close, we need that even more. If you will walk with God and fulfill His purpose, you will have no choice than to walk by faith. And if this year, we will dare new things and accomplish more for the Lord, there will be a greater demand on your faith in acting on God&rsquo;s word, in following the leading of the Holy Spirit, in giving for missions. You can&rsquo;t without faith. Remember: &ldquo;For we walk by faith, not by sight&rdquo; (2 Corinthians 5:7).</li>\r\n<li><strong>Be part of a local church:&nbsp;</strong>God is interested in us identifying with a local church where we are principally resident, a physical place where we can be nourished or have the opportunity to fellowship with other believers. Whatever God works in your life as an individual, is bound to multiply when you are also rightly situated with other believers. In this generation of telechurch, it is important to have a physical place to report to, a physical place where your absense can be recognized when you are not. You might just be suprised to discover what God has in store for you there, when you connect with other believers in your primary location. \"L<span>et us not neglect our meeting together, as some people do, but encourage one another, especially now that the day of his return is drawing near\" (Hebrews 10:25 NLT).</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is my prayer for you that indeed these words will be true for your life. That the Lord will bring to you increased revelations, fill you with the knowledge of His will and grace you for fulling His call. I also pray that He will multiply your substance and strategically position you for the revelation of His glory.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As you know, we are continually making sacrifices too financially to bring this word to many and to keep it available without a subscription fee for users on the app. This is also your opportunity to be part of a heavenly mission through your financial partnership. Among many projects for this year, we are building our website where you would be able to see the impact of this ministry and the difference we are making in many lives. These too entail cost. You are welcome to partner with us your partnership will be rewarded of God. For giving over PayPay, you can use the email address below for Lighthouse Global Missions. For information on alternative ways of giving, send us an email. Also write us with your feedback and testimonies. We are always glad to know what the word of God is accomplishing in your life.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God bless you.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pastor Simon</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">PayPal: <a href=\"mailto:pastorsimon@lgmissions.org\">pastorsimon@lgmissions.org</a><span> &nbsp;</span><span>(Receiver: Lighthouse Global Missions).</span></p>', '', '', 'news', '0', '1', '2024-01-06', '2024-01-06'),
(25, '1705506135.jpg', 'A SEASON OF DIVINE ANNOUNCEMENT', '', '', 'Pastor Simon Mungwa', '2017-01-24 03:42:15', '2024-01-17 03:42:15', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong></strong>Beloved in the Lord,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This season, God gave me a word for you. <strong>He said it will be a season of divine announcement, for God by Himself will be announcing His people in various places for the revelation of His glory.</strong> And I want to share with you the implications of this word.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Divine announcement is not a new concept. On the day Jesus was baptized, God Himself announced Jesus to the people saying: &ldquo;This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased!&rdquo; (Matthew 3:17). God also announced David to the prophet Samuel, to be anointed as King over Israel, while the young boy was busy tending the father&rsquo;s flock. David had nothing to do with that decision. It was God Himself who announced David to Samuel for a lifting. And this brings us to the implications of this word.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>GOD IS ANNOUNCING YOU TO ANGELIC HOSTS</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Angels are real and how we need them. The bible tells us angels are ministering spirits, they are servants sent to serve those who will inherit salvation (See Hebrews 1:14). And if you go through scriptures, their role could be seen from beginning to end. Their role in protecting God&rsquo;s people. On other occasions, they brought direction; and on other occasions, they brough resources as needed. They are also agents of war, waring, and overpowering forces of darkness, who otherwise would have prevailed in our lives. And this season, God is announcing you to angels, deploying angels on our behalf and sending them to work for His good purpose for us. Just as it is written: &ldquo;He will give His angels orders concerning you&rdquo; (See Psalm 91:11). This season, even if some things concern you where you think you have no one to help you, relax and know that God is deploying angels for you. He is announcing you to angelic host and giving them instructions for your good.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"2\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>GOD IS ANNOUNCING YOU TO MEN FOR LIFTING</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For Joseph to be appointed governor over the land of Egypt, someone had to mention him to the king. But it was all divinely orchestrated. Before this time, God had sent someone to Joseph whose dream was interpreted with accuracy. God would later give a dream to Pharoah that needed interpretation. And there was the servant to announce Joseph to the king. In effect, God announced Joseph in a foreign land, where he had no one to speak in his favor or defend his interest. If anything, his CV would have spoken against him. A foreign slave without education, who had attempted to rape the wife of an official. Even so God is putting us in the hearts of men this season, announcing us and shifting things for our lifting (See Genesis 41).</p>\r\n<ol start=\"3\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>GOD IS ANNOUNCING YOU TO AUTHORITIES</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We all get to deal with some authority at some point. It might be an employer or a government official who has something to do concerning our files or documents. Sometimes, authorities are like gate keepers who can either grant us access to something, or hinder us from coming through, particularly when it has to do with legality. But this is the word of the Lord concerning us this season and beyond. No authority will be able to stand against us and that which God is set to do. Be they authorities at our work or authorities in government. They cannot work against us. They can only work to our advantage. And this season, God is announcing us to the authorities to align with His purpose for us. As it is written: &ldquo;When they went from one nation to another, from one kingdom to another people, He permitted no one to do them wrong; yes, He rebuked kings for their sakes, saying, &lsquo;Do not touch My anointed ones, and do My prophets no harm&rsquo;&rdquo; (Psalm 105:13-15). And this is the injunction God has set for us. Irrespective of the authority, the Lord says to us as He said to Joshua: &ldquo;No one will be able to stand against you all the days of your life&rdquo; (Joshua 1:5).</p>\r\n<ol start=\"4\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>THE LORD IS ANNOUNCING US TO PRINCIPALITIES</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you think of Job, that will sound as a bad thing, because when God announced Job to Satan, it exposed the man to mishaps he would gladly have avoided. But this is different for us. God is announcing us to principalities and powers, so they know we are the King&rsquo;s kids. Just like Jesus, and Paul, principalities will know how to keep off when we show up. When the sons of Sceva went out facing some demons, the demons said to them: &ldquo;Jesus I know, and Paul I know about, but who are you?&rdquo; (Acts 19:15). We have the authority of Christ, and we are seated with Him in heavenly places above principalities and powers. And this season, there is an alarm sounded to them, to know and recognize your authority, and to bow to it.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This word came with one instruction for us: You should be prepared. You should be ready. For when God announces you, it is like turning on the spotlights on an individual. You don&rsquo;t want that light on you when you are not dressed and ready for it. For example, if you are trusting God for a promotion, be ready with your CV. If waiting for the bride or groom, carry yourself around like he or she is watching. You are working on a business; it is time to get things setup like you are ready for customers. Be ready for that which you are expecting, for God is shifting things already, He is announcing you. Hallelujah!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">And I pray indeed, that these prophetic words will be true for you. That God will announce you at various levels and cause good things to happen in your life, He will keep oppression far from you and increase your fortunes for His glory. In Jesus\' name. And now, let your \"Amen\" resound to the Lord!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We also want to give you opportunity to be part of this ministry work through your financial partnership as we bring the word of God to our generation and demonstrate acts of kindness to the needy in meeting their needs. We also have a website project underway and these all come with costs. For us to maintain the devotional content free on this app, it is through financial sacrifices of people like you. You can join the list today and become a partner. Be it a one-time offering or a commitment to a monthly or quarterly partnership, every gift goes a long way. You can directly give through PayPay using the address <a href=\"mailto:pastorsimon@lgmissions.org\">pastorsimon@lgmissions.org</a>. If you prefer giving differently, send me an email to same address and request additional information. Remember, your giving is to the Lord and He will greatly reward you with a multiplication (Luke 6:38).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God bless you!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Yours in Christ,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pastor Simon</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>', '', '', 'news', '0', '1', '2024-01-17', '2024-01-17'),
(26, '1716032113.jpg', 'A STORM IS COMING – a prophetic word for the season!', '', '', 'Pastor Simon Mungwa', '2018-05-24 11:26:48', '2024-05-18 11:51:57', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beloved of God, this season the Lord has given me a word for the times and a call to take refuge in Him as a matter of urgency. Now, for those who already have found refuge in Him, the call is to continue abiding in Him and be unshakable from that dwelling. And if someone has not yet done so, it only gets more dangerous to wait longer. For there is an approaching storm that calls for us to urgently take refuge.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a vision of the night, I saw the land being covered by the sudden appearance of very dark stormy clouds, even as the first drizzles already reached the ground. It was such dark clouds that were literally black, such as cast a shadow on everything and turned a bright day to sudden nightfall appearance. The clouds were so dark and thick, you could literally perceive it as mud that would drip from the skies &ndash; black clouds such as could not be visualized in nature. In this vision, for I had stepped out of the building for a given reason, I recognized the urgency to run to shelter. And as I headed into the house, another passerby ran off along with me to take shelter in the house, because she would not reach their destination before this dangerous storm caught up with her. It was such a fearful sight that one could wonder if the building would be any safe from the approaching storm. But once we were inside, it was a place of rest and comfort, we could nicely weather the storm if we stayed in.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;As I awoke from this vision, the word was clear to me! Even as it is written: For behold, <strong>&ldquo;The darkness shall cover the earth, and deep darkness the people&rdquo; (Isaiah 60:2).</strong> The times we are living in is a very prophetic season with unpleasant events in the earth. And it does not announce better days for humanity, unless by a divine intervention. And God wants to exclude us from the unpleasant experiences. Now, sometimes, people ask, why does God not just stop the events? He is not necessarily the author of them, and the earth is man&rsquo;s home. It is not as much His responsibility. However, He takes responsibility over those who bear His name. No doubt He spoke to the prophet saying: &ldquo;<strong><u>If my people, which are called by my name</u></strong>, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land&rdquo; (2 Chronicles 7:14).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Think of the state of emergency that takes place in a given country. Generally, when there is a sudden instability, foreign sovereign nations immediately call out for the evacuation of their citizens. Sometimes, they seek a safe exclusive place for their diplomats and citizens in that troubled nation until evacuation is possible. They have the obligation towards their own &ndash; not to everyone. In same way God seeks to deliver and preserve His own. Scripture says about God: <strong>&ldquo;The Lord knows those who are His.&rdquo;</strong> (2 Timothy 2:19).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There is a place of refuge God has provided for Humanity, and as many as run to it, will be saved and preserved from the storms that are coming. How it is written: <strong>&ldquo;The name of the LORD is a fortified tower; the righteous run to it and are safe&rdquo; (Proverbs 18:10).</strong> Then the Psalmists tells us of the one who takes refuge in the Lord: &ldquo;He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty. I will say of the Lord, He is my refuge and my fortress&hellip;&rdquo; And with much assuring words, He testifies: <strong>&ldquo;A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; but it shall not come nigh thee.&rdquo; (See Psalm 91).</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">That true place of security is in Christ. As simple as that is, it is a great truth. Christ is a person, but Christ is also a place. And in Him, like a cocoon shields a larva, so in Him we are shielded and excluded from the natural plagues of our world. How Paul wrote<strong>: &ldquo;Your life is hidden with Christ in God&rdquo;</strong> (See Colossians 3:3). He is that name which stands as a fortified tower, to which men run and are saved.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God is making a call to all men this season, to run to Jesus and take refuge from that which is coming. For no man can survive outside Christ &ndash; it is a hopeless choice to go for. The call is to accept Him as Lord and to receive and live in His word. Jesus Himself guaranteed: &ldquo;Therefore whoever hears these sayings of Mine, and does them, I will liken him to a wise man who built his house on the rock: and the rain descended, the floods came, and the winds blew and beat on that house; <strong><u>and it did not fall, for it was founded on the rock&rdquo;</u></strong> (Matthew 7:24-25). And finally, be led by the Holy Spirit. For He will lead you out of the paths of destruction into the ways of safety, bringing you to fields of green grass and refreshing pools of fresh water. For although darkness covers the earth, the glory of God is risen upon His people. Ours shall be a different story (See Isaiah 60:1-3).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When Jesus spoke of the times we are living in, He said: &ldquo;Men will faint from fear and anxiety over what is coming upon the earth&rdquo; (Luke 21:26). But that should not include us, for we have found a hiding place &ndash; a place of rest and comfort. It is a tower of refuge, tested and proven to be secured for all men. This also emphasizes the call we have to preach the gospel and to bring all men into God&rsquo;s place of refuge &ndash; Christ!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">And I pray for you in the name of Jesus, that the Lord will keep you and your loved ones, the Lord will guide you all and preserve you from every form of danger. And that you walk in His purpose and experience His goodness in the world.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Yours in Christ,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pastor Simon Mungwa</p>', '', '', 'news', '0', '1', '2024-05-18', '2024-05-18');
INSERT INTO `tbl_news` (`id`, `thumbnail`, `title`, `french_title`, `german_title`, `author`, `date`, `dmo`, `uti`, `utimo`, `content`, `french_content`, `german_content`, `type`, `views_count`, `cat_id`, `dou`, `init_date`) VALUES
(27, '1722673680.jpeg', 'A WELCOME NOTE from Pastor Simon', 'NOTE DE BIENVENUE du pasteur Simon', 'EIN WILLKOMMENSVERMERK von Pastor Simon', 'Pastor Simon Mungwa', '2027-06-24 03:11:44', '2024-08-03 08:28:00', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dear user of Your Daily Light app,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I am excited to welcome you on this mobile platform, established for your spiritual nourishment, even as it serves an ever-growing number of God&rsquo;s people around the world.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Your Daily Light is a divine idea. It is God&rsquo;s call to me to make His word available to His flock around the world across denominational boundaries, placing a portion of spiritual nourishment at their doorsteps daily. Just as Jesus said to Peter, <em><strong>&ldquo;Feed my sheep&rdquo;</strong></em> (John 21:17). So, I am excited to introduce to you Your Daily Light app which puts God&rsquo;s word in your hand on your mobile device anywhere you are in the world.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Paul prayed a prayer for the Church in Ephesus: <em><strong>&ldquo;I pray that the eyes of your heart may be enlightened, so that you will know what is the hope of His calling, what are the riches of the glory of His inheritance in the saints&rdquo;</strong> </em>(Ephesians 1:18). This is the purpose of your daily light. By the continual illumination through the scriptures, we shine the light on your path so you can know and walk in God&rsquo;s call for your life. We shine the light on you, so you can see who you are in Christ Jesus; and we shine the light on all that has been given to you in Christ, so you can take hold of them and live the fulfilling and victorious life that has been prearranged for you by God (See Ephesians 2:10).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This app is built to bring you more than just a devotional. In the Home section, you will find updates, news, testimonies, and a monthly prophetic word. The devotional section brings you daily inspiration, encouragement, guidance, illumination, and transformation in God&rsquo;s word. You can navigate to different days of devotionals by&nbsp; selecting the date at the top right hand in the devotional section. You will discover how to put the word of God to practical use and experience the supernatural presence and power of God on a daily basis.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our bookstore will feature books for your spiritual development and progress as the Lord inspires us and other authors to bring quality content to you. From your personal profile or the dropdown menu at the top, you can find opportunity to submit a prayer request, share a testimony and partner with us through your giving. There, you can also share the app and bring friends and family into this rich experience.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is my prayer that God will richly bless you and grace your life for a continuous glorious experience as you use Your Daily Light app. In Jesus&rsquo; name. Amen!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Welcome to an all-new experience with God&rsquo;s word.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>God bless you.</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pastor Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p>', '<p></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ch&egrave;re utilisatrice de l\'application Votre lumi&egrave;re du jour</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ch&egrave;re utilisatrice ou cher utilisateur de l\'application Votre lumi&egrave;re du jour,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Je suis heureux de vous accueillir sur cette plateforme mobile, &eacute;tablie pour votre nourriture spirituelle, m&ecirc;me si elle sert un nombre toujours croissant de personnes de Dieu &agrave; travers le monde.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Votre Lumi&egrave;re Quotidienne est une application qui a pour but de vous aider &agrave; mieux comprendre le monde dans lequel vous vivez.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Votre Lumi&egrave;re Quotidienne est une id&eacute;e divine. C\'est l\'appel que Dieu m\'a lanc&eacute; pour que je mette Sa parole &agrave; la disposition de Son troupeau dans le monde entier, au-del&agrave; des fronti&egrave;res confessionnelles, en d&eacute;posant chaque jour une portion de nourriture spirituelle &agrave; leur porte. Tout comme J&eacute;sus l\'a dit &agrave; Pierre, <em><strong>&ldquo;Pais mes brebis&rdquo;</strong></em> (Jean 21:17). C\'est pourquoi je suis heureux de vous pr&eacute;senter l\'application Votre lumi&egrave;re quotidienne qui met la parole de Dieu dans votre main sur votre appareil mobile, o&ugrave; que vous soyez dans le monde.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Paul a fait une pri&egrave;re pour l\'&Eacute;glise d\'&Eacute;ph&egrave;se : <em><strong>&ldquo;Je prie pour que les yeux de votre c&oelig;ur soient &eacute;clair&eacute;s, afin que vous sachiez quelle est l\'esp&eacute;rance de son appel, quelle est la richesse de la gloire de son h&eacute;ritage dans les saints&rdquo;</strong> </em>(&Eacute;ph&eacute;siens 1:18). Tel est le but de votre lumi&egrave;re quotidienne. Par l\'illumination continue des Ecritures, nous &eacute;clairons votre chemin afin que vous puissiez conna&icirc;tre l\'appel de Dieu pour votre vie et y marcher. Nous faisons briller la lumi&egrave;re sur vous, afin que vous puissiez voir qui vous &ecirc;tes dans le Christ J&eacute;sus ; et nous faisons briller la lumi&egrave;re sur tout ce qui vous a &eacute;t&eacute; donn&eacute; dans le Christ, afin que vous puissiez vous en emparer et vivre la vie &eacute;panouissante et victorieuse qui a &eacute;t&eacute; pr&eacute;par&eacute;e pour vous par Dieu (voir &Eacute;ph&eacute;siens 2:10).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Cette application est con&ccedil;ue pour vous apporter plus qu\'une simple d&eacute;votion. Dans la section Accueil, vous trouverez des mises &agrave; jour, des nouvelles, des t&eacute;moignages et une parole proph&eacute;tique mensuelle. La section d&eacute;votionnelle vous apporte chaque jour l\'inspiration, l\'encouragement, la guidance, l\'illumination et la transformation dans la parole de Dieu. Vous pouvez naviguer vers diff&eacute;rents jours de d&eacute;votion en s&eacute;lectionnant la date en haut &agrave; droite dans la section d&eacute;votionnelle. Vous d&eacute;couvrirez comment mettre la parole de Dieu en pratique et exp&eacute;rimenter la pr&eacute;sence et la puissance surnaturelles de Dieu au quotidien.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">La parole de Dieu, c\'est la vie, c\'est la vie.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Notre librairie proposera des livres pour votre d&eacute;veloppement spirituel et votre progr&egrave;s au fur et &agrave; mesure que le Seigneur nous inspire, ainsi que d\'autres auteurs, pour vous apporter un contenu de qualit&eacute;. Depuis votre profil personnel ou le menu d&eacute;roulant en haut de la page, vous avez la possibilit&eacute; de soumettre une demande de pri&egrave;re, de partager un t&eacute;moignage et de vous associer &agrave; nous par vos dons. Vous pouvez &eacute;galement partager l\'application et faire profiter vos amis et votre famille de cette exp&eacute;rience enrichissante.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">C\'est ma pri&egrave;re que Dieu vous b&eacute;nisse richement et gratifie votre vie d\'une exp&eacute;rience glorieuse continue lorsque vous utilisez l\'application Votre Lumi&egrave;re Quotidienne. Au nom de J&eacute;sus. Amen!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Bienvenue dans une toute nouvelle exp&eacute;rience avec la parole de Dieu.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pour une nouvelle exp&eacute;rience avec la parole de Dieu.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Dieu vous b&eacute;nisse.</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>La Parole de Dieu est une r&eacute;alit&eacute;.</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pasteur Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Dieu vous b&eacute;nit.</strong></p>', '<p></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Liebe Nutzer der Your Daily Light App,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ich freue mich, Sie auf dieser mobilen Plattform begr&uuml;&szlig;en zu d&uuml;rfen, die f&uuml;r Ihre geistliche Nahrung eingerichtet wurde, w&auml;hrend sie einer st&auml;ndig wachsenden Zahl von Gottes Volk auf der ganzen Welt dient.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Your Daily Light ist eine g&ouml;ttliche Idee. Es ist Gottes Ruf an mich, Sein Wort seiner Herde auf der ganzen Welt &uuml;ber konfessionelle Grenzen hinweg zug&auml;nglich zu machen und ihnen t&auml;glich eine Portion geistlicher Nahrung vor die Haust&uuml;r zu legen. Genau wie Jesus zu Petrus sagte: <em><strong>&ldquo;Weide meine Schafe&rdquo;</strong></em> (Johannes 21:17). Deshalb freue ich mich, Ihnen die App Your Daily Light vorzustellen, die Ihnen Gottes Wort auf Ihrem mobilen Ger&auml;t in die Hand gibt, egal wo auf der Welt Sie sich befinden.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Paulus betete ein Gebet f&uuml;r die Gemeinde in Ephesus: <em><strong>&ldquo;Ich bete, dass die Augen eures Herzens erleuchtet werden, damit ihr erkennt, was die Hoffnung seiner Berufung ist, was der Reichtum der Herrlichkeit seines Erbes in den Heiligen ist&rdquo;</strong> </em>(Epheser 1:18). Dies ist der Zweck eures t&auml;glichen Lichts. Durch die st&auml;ndige Erleuchtung durch die Heilige Schrift leuchten wir Ihnen den Weg, damit Sie Gottes Ruf f&uuml;r Ihr Leben erkennen und ihm folgen k&ouml;nnen. Wir leuchten auf dich, damit du erkennst, wer du in Christus Jesus bist; und wir leuchten auf alles, was dir in Christus geschenkt wurde, damit du es ergreifen und das erf&uuml;llte und siegreiche Leben leben kannst, das Gott f&uuml;r dich vorgesehen hat (siehe Epheser 2:10).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Diese App ist so aufgebaut, dass sie Ihnen mehr als nur eine Andacht bietet. In der Rubrik Home finden Sie aktuelle Informationen, Nachrichten, Zeugnisse und ein monatliches prophetisches Wort. Der Andachtsbereich bietet Ihnen t&auml;glich Inspiration, Ermutigung, F&uuml;hrung, Erleuchtung und Transformation durch Gottes Wort. Sie k&ouml;nnen zu den verschiedenen Tagen der Andachten navigieren, indem Sie das Datum oben rechts im Andachtsbereich ausw&auml;hlen. Sie werden entdecken, wie Sie das Wort Gottes praktisch anwenden und die &uuml;bernat&uuml;rliche Gegenwart und Kraft Gottes t&auml;glich erleben k&ouml;nnen.</p>\r\n<p>&gt;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Unsere Buchhandlung wird B&uuml;cher f&uuml;r Ihre geistliche Entwicklung und Ihren Fortschritt anbieten, wenn der Herr uns und andere Autoren dazu inspiriert, Ihnen qualitativ hochwertige Inhalte zu liefern. In Ihrem pers&ouml;nlichen Profil oder im Dropdown-Men&uuml; oben finden Sie die M&ouml;glichkeit, ein Gebetsanliegen einzureichen, ein Zeugnis zu teilen und uns durch Ihre Spenden zu unterst&uuml;tzen. Dort k&ouml;nnen Sie die App auch teilen und Freunde und Familie an dieser reichen Erfahrung teilhaben lassen.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Es ist mein Gebet, dass Gott Sie reich segnet und Ihr Leben mit einer fortw&auml;hrenden herrlichen Erfahrung beschenkt, w&auml;hrend Sie die App Your Daily Light nutzen. In Jesus&rsquo; Namen. Amen!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Willkommen zu einer ganz neuen Erfahrung mit Gottes Wort.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Gott segne Sie.</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pastor Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p>', 'news', '0', '1', '2024-06-27', '2024-06-27'),
(28, '1743365482.jpg', '2025: THE YEAR OF THE KINGDOM LIFE', '2025 : L\'ANNÉE DE LA VIE DANS LE ROYAUME', '2025: DAS JAHR DES KÖNIGLICHEN LEBENS', 'Simon T. Mungwa', '2030-03-25 08:11:19', '2025-03-30 08:11:22', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There are times and seasons when the Lord is accomplishing a set work in our lives and in our world. And in this season, He wants us to be aligned with His purpose so that we can make the most of the times. While the start of these divine seasons might not always coincide with the beginning of the year, God does take pleasure in making the beginning of a new year the start of new seasons. This is the reason we receive a word for the year by which we should run. Much like it is written: &ldquo;Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lord&rsquo;s will is&rdquo; (Ephesians 5:17 NIV).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This year 2025, the word the Lord put on my heart for His people is this: It is &ldquo;The year of the Kingdom Life.&rdquo; If you have been following Your Daily Light devotional for 2025, you would have known this from the first day of the year. And through the devotionals that have followed, every communication has been in line with this word: bringing illumination on the Kingdom Life, what that means for you and how you can make it a reality for yourself.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When Jesus sent the disciples, He gave theme these instructions: &ldquo;Whatever city you enter, and they receive you, eat such things as are set before you.&nbsp; And heal the sick there, and say to them, &ldquo;The kingdom of God has come near to you.&ldquo;&nbsp; (Luke 10:8-9). When you go through scriptures and consider the ministry of Jesus, you recognize His message was really about the Kingdom of God and the life thereof. And even when He commissioned the disciples, it was about the Kingdom.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is more than the message of a religion or simply becoming born again. Central to it was the Kingdom of God and the life thereof. And this is the purpose of this word for the year. This has great implications: There is a kingdom we have been brought into; a government, whose purpose we should serve; a supernatural life characteristic of the Kingdom that we should live; a glory, divine power and heavenly authority to experience &ndash; such as bring us into the full manifestations as sons of God. How it is indeed written, that all of creation wait for the manifestation of the sons of God. (See Romans 8:19). And this word is for us, and the time is now to manifest the kingdom life and reveal the Father&rsquo;s glory to all. And particularly, this year, God is calling us back to the message of the gospel of the Kingdom, and the life thereof, lived and expressed in full divine glory, kingdom power and heavenly authority!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the follow up message, I will share with you five things God expects of you in this year, so that you can be fully aligned with His purpose and experience the fulness of His blessings for you in this season and beyond.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I pray that this word will be true for your life, that you will walk into the real experience of the Kingdom and the life thereof, having great intimacy and experiences with God through the person of the Holy Spirit, and showcasing the glory, the power and the virtues of the life in Christ. In Jesus name.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God bless you,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Send me a personal&nbsp;message</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Email: <a href=\"mailto:PastorSimon@lgmissions.org\">PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</a></strong></p>', '<p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Il y a des temps et des saisons où le Seigneur accomplit une œuvre déterminée dans nos vies et dans notre monde. Et dans cette saison, il veut que nous soyons alignés sur son dessein afin que nous puissions tirer le meilleur parti de ces moments. Bien que le début de ces saisons divines ne coïncide pas toujours avec le début de l\'année, Dieu prend plaisir à faire du début d\'une nouvelle année le début de nouvelles saisons. C\'est la raison pour laquelle nous recevons un mot pour l\'année que nous devons suivre. Comme il est écrit : &ldquo;Ne soyez donc pas stupides, mais comprenez quelle est la volonté du Seigneur&rdquo ; (Ephésiens 5:17 NIV).</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Les mots de l\'année sont des mots de l\'année, que nous devrions suivre.\r\n</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">En cette année 2025, la parole que le Seigneur a mise sur mon cœur pour son peuple est la suivante : C\'est &ldquo;L\'année de la Vie du Royaume.&rdquo;Si vous avez suivi la dévotion de Votre Lumière Quotidienne pour 2025, vous l\'avez su dès le premier jour de l\'année. Et à travers les dévotionnels qui ont suivi, chaque communication a été en ligne avec ce mot : apporter une illumination sur la Vie du Royaume, ce que cela signifie pour vous et comment vous pouvez en faire une réalité pour vous-même.</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">L\'année 2025 est l\'année de la vie du Royaume.\r\n</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Lorsque Jésus a envoyé les disciples, il leur a donné ces instructions : &ldquo;Dans quelque ville que vous entriez, et où l\'on vous recevra, mangez de ce qui vous sera présenté.&nbsp ; Guérissez-y les malades, et dites-leur : &ldquo;Le royaume de Dieu s\'est approché de vous.&nbsp ; (Luc 10:8-9). Lorsque l\'on parcourt les Écritures et que l\'on examine le ministère de Jésus, on s\'aperçoit que son message concernait réellement le Royaume de Dieu et la vie qui en découle. Et même lorsqu\'il a chargé ses disciples de la mission, il s\'agissait du Royaume.\r\n</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Ce n\'est pas seulement le message d\'une religion ou le simple fait de naître de nouveau. Il s\'agit avant tout du Royaume de Dieu et de la vie qui en découle. Et c\'est l\'objectif de ce mot de l\'année. Cela a de grandes implications : Il y a un royaume dans lequel nous avons été introduits, un gouvernement que nous devons servir, une vie surnaturelle caractéristique du Royaume que nous devons vivre, une gloire, une puissance divine et une autorité céleste à expérimenter &ndash, qui nous amènent à nous manifester pleinement en tant que fils de Dieu. Il est en effet écrit que toute la création attend la manifestation des fils de Dieu. (Voir Romains 8:19). Et cette parole est pour nous, et le temps est venu de manifester la vie du royaume et de révéler la gloire du Père à tous. En particulier, cette année, Dieu nous appelle à revenir au message de l\'Évangile du Royaume, et à la vie qui en découle, vécue et exprimée dans la pleine gloire divine, la puissance du Royaume et l\'autorité céleste !</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">La vie du Royaume est pour nous.\r\n</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Dans le message suivant, je partagerai avec vous cinq choses que Dieu attend de vous au cours de cette année, afin que vous puissiez être pleinement alignés sur son dessein et expérimenter la plénitude de ses bénédictions pour vous au cours de cette saison et au-delà.</p>\r\n</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Je prie pour que cette parole soit vraie pour votre vie, que vous marchiez dans l\'expérience réelle du Royaume et de sa vie, en ayant une grande intimité et des expériences avec Dieu à travers la personne du Saint-Esprit, et en montrant la gloire, la puissance et les vertus de la vie en Christ. Au nom de Jésus.</p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Jésus\r\n<p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Dieu vous bénisse,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong>Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Simon T. Mungwa</strong><p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong></strong></p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong></strong></p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong\r\n<p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong>Envoyez-moi un message personnel</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong>Envoyez-moi un message personnel\r\n<p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"><strong>Email : <a href=\"mailto:PastorSimon@lgmissions.org\">PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</a></strong></p> <p style=\"text-align : justify ;\">Envoyer un message personnel', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Es gibt Zeiten und Jahreszeiten, in denen der Herr ein bestimmtes Werk in unserem Leben und in unserer Welt vollbringt. Und in dieser Zeit möchte er, dass wir uns auf sein Ziel ausrichten, damit wir das Beste aus dieser Zeit machen können. Auch wenn der Beginn dieser göttlichen Jahreszeiten nicht immer mit dem Jahresbeginn zusammenfällt, hat Gott doch seine Freude daran, den Beginn eines neuen Jahres zum Beginn neuer Jahreszeiten zu machen. Aus diesem Grund erhalten wir ein Wort für das Jahr, nach dem wir laufen sollen. So wie es geschrieben steht: &ldquo;Darum seid nicht töricht, sondern versteht, was der Wille des Herrn ist&rdquo; (Epheser 5:17 NIV).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dieses Jahr 2025 ist das Wort, das der Herr mir für sein Volk aufs Herz gelegt hat: Es ist &ldquo;Das Jahr des Lebens im Reich Gottes. &rdquo; Wenn Sie die Andachten von Your Daily Light für 2025 verfolgt haben, wussten Sie das schon am ersten Tag des Jahres. Und in den darauffolgenden Andachten war jede Mitteilung auf dieses Wort ausgerichtet: Erleuchtung über das Leben im Reich Gottes, was das für Sie bedeutet und wie Sie es für sich selbst verwirklichen können.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Als Jesus die Jünger aussandte, gab er ihnen folgende Anweisungen: &ldquo;In welche Stadt ihr auch kommt, und sie nehmen euch auf, so esst, was euch vorgesetzt wird.&nbsp; Und heilt dort die Kranken und sprecht zu ihnen: &ldquo;Das Reich Gottes ist nahe zu euch gekommen.&ldquo;&nbsp; (Lukas 10:8-9). Wenn man die Bibelstellen durchgeht und den Dienst Jesu betrachtet, erkennt man, dass es in seiner Botschaft wirklich um das Reich Gottes und das Leben darin ging. Und selbst als er die Jünger beauftragte, ging es um das Reich Gottes.</p>>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dies ist mehr als die Botschaft einer Religion oder einer einfachen Wiedergeburt. Im Mittelpunkt stand das Reich Gottes und das Leben darin. Und das ist das Ziel dieses Wortes für dieses Jahr. Das hat große Auswirkungen: Es gibt ein Reich, in das wir hineingebracht wurden; eine Regierung, deren Zweck wir dienen sollen; ein übernatürliches Leben, das für das Reich Gottes charakteristisch ist und das wir leben sollen; eine Herrlichkeit, göttliche Macht und himmlische Autorität, die wir erfahren sollen &ndash; solche, die uns in die volle Offenbarung als Söhne Gottes bringen. Es steht ja geschrieben, dass die ganze Schöpfung auf die Offenbarung der Söhne Gottes wartet. (Siehe Römer 8,19). Und dieses Wort gilt uns, und die Zeit ist jetzt, das Leben im Reich Gottes zu manifestieren und die Herrlichkeit des Vaters allen zu offenbaren. Und besonders in diesem Jahr ruft Gott uns zurück zur Botschaft des Evangeliums vom Reich Gottes und dem Leben daraus, das in voller göttlicher Herrlichkeit, in königlicher Macht und himmlischer Autorität gelebt und zum Ausdruck gebracht wird.\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In der Folgebotschaft werde ich Ihnen fünf Dinge mitteilen, die Gott in diesem Jahr von Ihnen erwartet, damit Sie voll und ganz auf seine Absicht ausgerichtet sind und die Fülle seiner Segnungen für Sie in dieser Jahreszeit und darüber hinaus erleben können.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ich bete dafür, dass dieses Wort für dein Leben gilt, dass du in die wahre Erfahrung des Reiches Gottes und seines Lebens eintrittst, dass du durch die Person des Heiligen Geistes große Intimität und Erfahrungen mit Gott machst und die Herrlichkeit, die Macht und die Tugenden des Lebens in Christus zur Schau stellst. In Jesu Namen.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Gott segne Sie,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Simon T. Mungwa</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Senden Sie mir eine persönliche&nbsp;Nachricht</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Email: <a href=\"mailto:PastorSimon@lgmissions.org\">PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</a></strong></p>', 'news', '0', '1', '2025-03-30', '2025-03-30');
INSERT INTO `tbl_news` (`id`, `thumbnail`, `title`, `french_title`, `german_title`, `author`, `date`, `dmo`, `uti`, `utimo`, `content`, `french_content`, `german_content`, `type`, `views_count`, `cat_id`, `dou`, `init_date`) VALUES
(29, '1747345846.jpg', 'ALIGN WITH THE PROPHETIC WORD', 'S\'ALIGNER SUR LA PAROLE PROPHÉTIQUE', 'RICHTET EUCH NACH DEM PROPHETISCHEN WORT', 'Simon T. Mungwa', '2015-05-25 09:50:42', '2025-05-15 09:57:51', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As with many prophetic messages, there are often accompanying instructions to help position us correctly so that we can be in the right disposition for the full experience of that which the Lord has spoken. For this year, as a ministry, the word we have received from the Lord is that this year 2025 is &ldquo;The year of the Kingdom Life&rdquo;. In a previous post, we emphasized what that really meant and what we ought to expect. In this post, I am writing to share with you five core areas you would have to give attention to in this year of the Kingdom life, in order to be fully aligned with God and to have the full experience of the blessings wrapped in the season and beyond.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>UNDERSTAND THE KINGDOM AND THE LIFE THEREOF</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There is a Kingdom, a real one into which we have been born when we received Christ. It is the Kingdom of light, the kingdom of God&rsquo;s beloved son (See John 3:5-6 and Colossians 1:12). Like every environment it is important to recognize where you are and understand the operations and laws of that environment. Only then can you harness everything to work for your advantage. There is also a placement for you, a position you occupy. By knowing where you are, who you are, what resources are at your disposal, what other entities or personalities make up your world and how they impact your life, you are able to make the most of your environment, function at your best and get the best results. And that is the emphasis for you, to increase in your knowledge of the Kingdom and the life thereof. So you can fully live the Kingdom life. It is written of Jesus after His resurrection, &ldquo;He also presented Himself alive after His suffering by many infallible proofs, being seen by them during forty days <u>and speaking of the things pertaining to the kingdom of God&rdquo; (Acts 1:3)</u>. How much do you know about the things &nbsp;of the Kingdom of God and how well do you live the Kingdom life?</p>\r\n<ol start=\"2\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>PRIORITIZE THE KINGDOM</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This year, every need is literally guaranteed to be met. In fact, we can spare ourselves the worry if we would just get our priorities right. And that is an instruction for this season and beyond. To prioritize the Kingdom of God, that means to set its purpose, its mission, its values, goals and culture above everything else. Like Jesus guaranteed: &ldquo;Seek first the kingdom of God and His righteousness, and all these things shall be added to you&rdquo; (Matthew 6:33). When Jesus said, &ldquo;All these things..&rdquo;, he referred to the basic necessities of life, such things for which the rest of the world toil day and night, seeking to get for a comfortable and enjoyable life. All that is ours and more in Christ Jesus, much so in this year of the Kingdom life, if we would seek the Kingdom above all else.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"3\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>SERVE KINGDOM PURPOSE</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God has a purpose for your life; God has a kingdom purpose to which your life is also connected. And this year of the Kingdom life, He calls you to recognize this more than ever before and be about Kingdom purpose. You can easily live for yourself, or for your family. But there is a better way to live and a greater purpose to live for. That is to serve Kingdom purpose. How He causes all things to work for the good of them that love Him and are called ACCORDING TO HIS PURPOSE (See Romans 8:28). A lot to share on this subject, but this is not the avenue. How Mordecai said to Esther, &ldquo;Who knows whether you have come to the kingdom for such a time as this?&rdquo; (Esther 4:14). Even so there is a purpose for you to serve in the Kingdom, and that you should get committed to like never before.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"4\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>PROPAGATE THE GOSPEL OF THE KINGDOM</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Jesus once said: &ldquo;This gospel of the kingdom will be preached in all the world as a witness to all the nations, and then the end will come&rdquo; (Matthew 24:14). And this is top priority in the kingdom, to get the good news to everyone in every place. And you have something to do about it. Get involved, share the good news of the Kingdom with those around you, your friends, neighbors, colleagues, and everyone you could have audience with and the opportunity to speak to about Jesus. Let them know of the King, his love for them, His invitation to them, and the Kingdom prepared for them. Let them know Jesus is the way. Someday, God will hold each of us to account for them that were assigned to hear the gospel through us. You want to be that faithful servant who did the Father&rsquo;s will. Sometimes all you need to do is invite someone to a kingdom event or give them a free copy of such content that conveys the message of the gospel like a copy of Your Daily Light. You can also simply share the link to the mobile app with someone to download. All that is part of propagating the gospel.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"5\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>INVEST IN KINGDOM ADVANCEMENT</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As part of the prophecies concerning Jesus, the Prophet Isaiah declared: &ldquo;To the increase of His kingdom shall be no end&rdquo; (Isaiah 9:6). God has an agenda of advancing His Kingdom and establishing His reign in every facet of life. He seeks to establish his reign in every land, in every government, in every institution and in every life. This is only possible through the continuous work of missions in reaching men for the Lord. This entails cost on many fronts. And God is inviting us to invest our time and our resources more than ever before in Kingdom advancement, supporting ministries and enabling ministers to be more effective in His service. And this is the best return on investment you could ever get, when you invest&nbsp;&nbsp; in kingdom advancement.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How Jesus said, do not lay up for yourself treasures on earth where moth and rust destroy, and thieves break in to steal. He said, lay up your treasures in heaven where they are eternally secured. Even more, He guaranteed us a hundredfold return of whatever we forgo for His purpose, in this live, and in the life to come, eternal life. This year, therefore, you should be even more intentional about giving for Kingdom advancement. It is not time to relax if you have been doing that. It is time to multiply your commitment and give even more sacrificially (See Matthew 6:19-20 and Mark 10:29-30).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is the call we are fulfilling as Lighthouse Global Missions in advancing God&rsquo;s Kingdom, just like many other ministries. We are using many avenues to bring the Word of God to people around the world. Through ministry events, philanthropic outreach, the publication and distribution of illuminating material in book format, or through our mobile application accessible around the world. We are making great sacrifices financially to make this possible. And you too can be a part. Even as you act on this word of investing for Kingdom advancement, you should consider partnership with Lighthouse Global Missions through giving. You will be joining us in amplifying our impact as a mission.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This year of the kingdom life, there is so much to explore, so much to grow into, even as God causes His power and glory to be revealed in our lives in an unprecedented manner. As part of your responsibility to be aligned, you have the above five aspects to give attention to. Also do well to follow through our journey this year with Your Daily Light devotionals. For through its content, you will gain great insights into the kingdom life and make that a living reality for yourself.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It is my prayer, that God&rsquo;s grace will be richly multiplied in your life and He will cause you to prosper in all things as is <strong>characteristic of the Kingdom Life</strong>. In Jesus&rsquo; name.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">God bless you</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With the love of God,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Send me a personal email at&nbsp;PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">share your feedback and testimonies. You can also let me know how I can pray for you.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Comme pour beaucoup de messages proph&eacute;tiques, il y a souvent des instructions qui les accompagnent pour nous aider &agrave; nous positionner correctement afin que nous puissions &ecirc;tre dans la bonne disposition pour la pleine exp&eacute;rience de ce que le Seigneur a dit. Pour cette ann&eacute;e, en tant que minist&egrave;re, la parole que nous avons re&ccedil;ue du Seigneur est que cette ann&eacute;e 2025 est &ldquo;L\'ann&eacute;e de la Vie du Royaume&amp;rdquo ;. Dans un billet pr&eacute;c&eacute;dent, nous avons soulign&eacute; ce que cela signifiait r&eacute;ellement et ce &agrave; quoi nous devions nous attendre. Dans ce billet, j\'&eacute;cris pour partager avec vous cinq domaines fondamentaux auxquels vous devriez pr&ecirc;ter attention en cette ann&eacute;e de la vie du Royaume, afin d\'&ecirc;tre pleinement align&eacute; avec Dieu et d\'avoir la pleine exp&eacute;rience des b&eacute;n&eacute;dictions envelopp&eacute;es dans la saison et au-del&agrave;.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Seul le texte de l\'article est disponible en anglais.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>CONNA&Icirc;TRE LE ROYAUME ET LA VIE QUI EN D&Eacute;COULENT</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Il y a un Royaume, un vrai, dans lequel nous sommes n&eacute;s en recevant le Christ. C\'est le Royaume de lumi&egrave;re, le Royaume du fils bien-aim&eacute; de Dieu (voir Jean 3,5-6 et Colossiens 1,12). Comme pour tout environnement, il est important de savoir o&ugrave; l\'on se trouve et de comprendre le fonctionnement et les lois de cet environnement. Ce n\'est qu\'alors que vous pourrez tout exploiter &agrave; votre avantage. Il y a aussi une place pour vous, une position que vous occupez. En sachant o&ugrave; vous &ecirc;tes, qui vous &ecirc;tes, quelles sont les ressources &agrave; votre disposition, quelles sont les autres entit&eacute;s ou personnalit&eacute;s qui composent votre monde et comment elles influencent votre vie, vous &ecirc;tes en mesure de tirer le meilleur parti de votre environnement, de fonctionner au mieux et d\'obtenir les meilleurs r&eacute;sultats. Et c\'est l&agrave; l\'essentiel pour vous : accro&icirc;tre votre connaissance du Royaume et de la vie qui s\'y rattache. Ainsi, vous pourrez vivre pleinement la vie du Royaume. Il est &eacute;crit de J&eacute;sus apr&egrave;s sa r&eacute;surrection, &ldquo;Il s\'est aussi pr&eacute;sent&eacute; vivant apr&egrave;s ses souffrances par plusieurs preuves infaillibles, se faisant voir d\'eux pendant quarante jours <u>et parlant des choses qui concernent le royaume de Dieu&amp;rdquo ; (Actes 1:3)</u>. Que savez-vous des choses &nbsp;du Royaume de Dieu et dans quelle mesure vivez-vous la vie du Royaume ?</p>\r\n<ol start=\"2\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>PRIORISER LE ROYAUME</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Cette ann&eacute;e, tous les besoins sont litt&eacute;ralement assur&eacute;s d\'&ecirc;tre satisfaits. En fait, nous pouvons nous &eacute;pargner des soucis si nous parvenons &agrave; mettre de l\'ordre dans nos priorit&eacute;s. C\'est une consigne pour cette saison et au-del&agrave;. Donner la priorit&eacute; au Royaume de Dieu, cela signifie placer son but, sa mission, ses valeurs, ses objectifs et sa culture au-dessus de tout le reste. Comme J&eacute;sus l\'a garanti : \"Cherchez d\'abord le royaume de Dieu et sa justice, et toutes ces choses vous seront donn&eacute;es par surcro&icirc;t\" (Matthieu 6:33). Lorsque J&eacute;sus a dit \"toutes ces choses\", il faisait r&eacute;f&eacute;rence aux n&eacute;cessit&eacute;s de base de la vie, ces choses pour lesquelles le reste du monde travaille jour et nuit, cherchant &agrave; les obtenir pour mener une vie confortable et agr&eacute;able. Tout cela est &agrave; nous et plus encore dans le Christ J&eacute;sus, surtout en cette ann&eacute;e de la vie du Royaume, si nous cherchons le Royaume par-dessus tout.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Les mots \"le Royaume\" et \"la vie\" ne sont pas toujours les m&ecirc;mes.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"3\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>SERVIR LE BUT DU ROYAUME</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dieu a un but pour votre vie ; Dieu a un but pour le Royaume auquel votre vie est &eacute;galement li&eacute;e. En cette ann&eacute;e de la vie dans le Royaume, il vous appelle &agrave; le reconna&icirc;tre plus que jamais et &agrave; vous consacrer &agrave; l\'objectif du Royaume. Vous pouvez facilement vivre pour vous-m&ecirc;me ou pour votre famille. Mais il y a une meilleure fa&ccedil;on de vivre et un but plus grand pour lequel vivre. Il s\'agit de servir l\'objectif du Royaume. Il fait concourir toutes choses au bien de ceux qui l\'aiment et qui sont appel&eacute;s SELON SON DESSEIN (voir Romains 8:28). Il y aurait beaucoup &agrave; partager sur ce sujet, mais ce n\'est pas l\'occasion. Comme Mardoch&eacute;e a dit &agrave; Esther, &ldquo;Qui sait si tu es venue dans le royaume pour un temps comme celui-ci?&amp;rdquo ; (Esther 4:14). Quoi qu\'il en soit, il y a pour vous un but &agrave; servir dans le Royaume, et vous devriez vous y engager comme jamais auparavant.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"4\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>PROPAGER L\'&Eacute;VANGILE DU ROYAUME</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">J&eacute;sus a dit un jour : &ldquo;Cette bonne nouvelle du royaume sera pr&ecirc;ch&eacute;e dans le monde entier, pour servir de t&eacute;moignage &agrave; toutes les nations, et alors viendra la fin&amp;rdquo ; (Matthieu 24:14). C\'est la priorit&eacute; absolue du royaume : transmettre la bonne nouvelle &agrave; tout le monde et en tout lieu. Et vous avez quelque chose &agrave; faire &agrave; ce sujet. Impliquez-vous, partagez la bonne nouvelle du Royaume avec ceux qui vous entourent, vos amis, vos voisins, vos coll&egrave;gues, et tous ceux que vous pourriez rencontrer et &agrave; qui vous pourriez parler de J&eacute;sus. Faites-leur conna&icirc;tre le Roi, son amour pour eux, son invitation et le Royaume pr&eacute;par&eacute; pour eux. Faites-leur savoir que J&eacute;sus est le chemin. Un jour, Dieu demandera &agrave; chacun d\'entre nous de rendre compte de ceux qui ont &eacute;t&eacute; charg&eacute;s d\'entendre l\'&Eacute;vangile par notre interm&eacute;diaire. Vous voulez &ecirc;tre ce serviteur fid&egrave;le qui a fait la volont&eacute; du P&egrave;re. Parfois, il suffit d\'inviter quelqu\'un &agrave; un &eacute;v&eacute;nement du royaume ou de lui donner un exemplaire gratuit d\'un contenu qui transmet le message de l\'&Eacute;vangile, comme un exemplaire de Votre lumi&egrave;re quotidienne. Vous pouvez aussi simplement partager le lien vers l\'application mobile avec quelqu\'un pour qu\'il la t&eacute;l&eacute;charge. Tout cela fait partie de la propagation de l\'&Eacute;vangile.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"5\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>INVESTIR DANS L\'AVANCEMENT DU ROYAUME</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dans le cadre des proph&eacute;ties concernant J&eacute;sus, le proph&egrave;te Isa&iuml;e a d&eacute;clar&eacute; : &ldquo;Il n\'y aura pas de fin &agrave; l\'accroissement de son r&egrave;gne&amp;rdquo ; (Isa&iuml;e 9:6). Dieu a pour objectif de faire progresser son royaume et d\'&eacute;tablir son r&egrave;gne dans tous les domaines de la vie. Il cherche &agrave; &eacute;tablir son r&egrave;gne dans chaque pays, dans chaque gouvernement, dans chaque institution et dans chaque vie. Cela n\'est possible que par le travail continu des missions pour atteindre les hommes pour le Seigneur. Cela implique des co&ucirc;ts sur de nombreux fronts. Et Dieu nous invite &agrave; investir plus que jamais notre temps et nos ressources dans l\'avancement du Royaume, en soutenant les minist&egrave;res et en permettant aux ministres d\'&ecirc;tre plus efficaces &agrave; son service. Et c\'est l&agrave; le meilleur retour sur investissement que vous puissiez jamais obtenir, lorsque vous investissez dans l\'avancement du Royaume.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Comme l\'a dit J&eacute;sus, ne vous amassez pas des tr&eacute;sors sur la terre, o&ugrave; la teigne et la rouille d&eacute;truisent, et o&ugrave; les voleurs s\'introduisent pour voler. Il a dit : amassez vos tr&eacute;sors au ciel, o&ugrave; ils seront &eacute;ternellement en s&eacute;curit&eacute;. Plus encore, il nous a garanti le retour au centuple de tout ce &agrave; quoi nous renon&ccedil;ons pour servir ses desseins, dans cette vie et dans la vie &agrave; venir, la vie &eacute;ternelle. Cette ann&eacute;e, par cons&eacute;quent, vous devriez &ecirc;tre encore plus attentifs &agrave; donner pour l\'avancement du Royaume. Ce n\'est pas le moment de vous rel&acirc;cher si vous l\'avez d&eacute;j&agrave; fait. Il est temps de multiplier votre engagement et de donner de mani&egrave;re encore plus sacrificielle (voir Matthieu 6:19-20 et Marc 10:29-30).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">La vie &eacute;ternelle.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">C\'est l\'appel que nous remplissons en tant que Lighthouse Global Missions pour faire avancer le Royaume de Dieu, comme beaucoup d\'autres minist&egrave;res. Nous utilisons de nombreux moyens pour apporter la Parole de Dieu aux gens du monde entier. Par le biais d\'&eacute;v&eacute;nements minist&eacute;riels, d\'activit&eacute;s philanthropiques, de la publication et de la distribution de mat&eacute;riel &eacute;clairant sous forme de livre, ou par le biais de notre application mobile accessible partout dans le monde. Nous faisons de grands sacrifices financiers pour rendre cela possible. Et vous aussi, vous pouvez y participer. Tout en agissant sur cette parole d\'investissement pour l\'avancement du Royaume, vous devriez envisager un partenariat avec Lighthouse Global Missions par le biais d\'un don. Vous vous joindrez &agrave; nous pour amplifier notre impact en tant que mission.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lighthouse Global Missions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Cette ann&eacute;e de la vie dans le royaume, il y a tant de choses &agrave; explorer, tant de choses dans lesquelles grandir, alors m&ecirc;me que Dieu fait en sorte que sa puissance et sa gloire se r&eacute;v&egrave;lent dans nos vies d\'une mani&egrave;re sans pr&eacute;c&eacute;dent. Dans le cadre de votre responsabilit&eacute; d\'&ecirc;tre align&eacute;, vous devez pr&ecirc;ter attention aux cinq aspects ci-dessus. Vous feriez &eacute;galement bien de suivre notre voyage de cette ann&eacute;e avec les d&eacute;votionnels de Votre Lumi&egrave;re Quotidienne. En effet, gr&acirc;ce &agrave; son contenu, vous aurez un aper&ccedil;u de la vie dans le royaume et vous pourrez en faire une r&eacute;alit&eacute; vivante pour vous-m&ecirc;me.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">La vie dans le royaume, c\'est la vie dans le royaume.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">C\'est ma pri&egrave;re que la gr&acirc;ce de Dieu soit richement multipli&eacute;e dans votre vie et qu\'Il vous fasse prosp&eacute;rer en toutes choses comme cela est <strong>caract&eacute;ristique de la vie du Royaume</strong>. Au nom de J&eacute;sus&rsquo;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">J&eacute;sus&rsquo;nom.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dieu vous b&eacute;nit</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dieu vous b&eacute;nit</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Avec l\'amour de Dieu,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">La vie du Royaume</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">L\'amour de Dieu.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Envoyez-moi un courriel personnel &agrave;&nbsp;PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">partagez vos commentaires et t&eacute;moignages. Vous pouvez &eacute;galement me faire savoir comment je peux prier pour vous.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Parlez-moi de vos r&eacute;actions et de vos t&eacute;moignages.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">p style=\"text-align : justify ;\"&gt;</p>\r\n<p></p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">RICHTET EUCH NACH DEM PROPHETISCHEN WORT</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Wie bei vielen prophetischen Botschaften gibt es oft Anweisungen, die uns helfen, uns richtig zu positionieren, damit wir in der richtigen Verfassung sind, um das, was der Herr gesagt hat, voll und ganz zu erleben. F&uuml;r dieses Jahr haben wir als Dienst vom Herrn das Wort erhalten, dass dieses Jahr 2025 &bdquo;das Jahr des Lebens im K&ouml;nigreich&ldquo; ist. In einem fr&uuml;heren Beitrag haben wir betont, was das wirklich bedeutet und was wir erwarten sollten. In diesem Beitrag m&ouml;chte ich euch f&uuml;nf Kernbereiche vorstellen, auf die ihr in diesem Jahr des K&ouml;nigreichslebens achten solltet, um ganz auf Gott ausgerichtet zu sein und die Segnungen dieser Zeit und dar&uuml;ber hinaus in vollem Umfang zu erfahren.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>VERSTEHE DAS REICH UND DAS LEBEN DARIN</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Es gibt ein Reich, ein echtes Reich, in das wir hineingeboren wurden, als wir Christus angenommen haben. Es ist das Reich des Lichts, das Reich des geliebten Sohnes Gottes (siehe Johannes 3,5-6 und Kolosser 1,12). Wie in jeder Umgebung ist es wichtig zu erkennen, wo du bist, und die Funktionsweise und Gesetze dieser Umgebung zu verstehen. Nur dann kannst du alles zu deinem Vorteil nutzen. Es gibt auch einen Platz f&uuml;r dich, eine Position, die du einnimmst. Wenn du wei&szlig;t, wo du bist, wer du bist, welche Ressourcen dir zur Verf&uuml;gung stehen, welche anderen Wesenheiten oder Pers&ouml;nlichkeiten deine Welt ausmachen und wie sie dein Leben beeinflussen, kannst du das Beste aus deiner Umgebung machen, deine besten Leistungen erbringen und die besten Ergebnisse erzielen. Und genau darauf liegt der Schwerpunkt f&uuml;r dich: dein Wissen &uuml;ber das K&ouml;nigreich und das Leben darin zu erweitern. So kannst du das Leben im Reich Gottes in vollen Z&uuml;gen genie&szlig;en. &Uuml;ber Jesus steht nach seiner Auferstehung geschrieben: &bdquo;Er zeigte sich nach seinem Leiden durch viele untr&uuml;gliche Beweise als der Lebendige und erschien ihnen vierzig Tage lang und redete mit ihnen &uuml;ber das Reich Gottes&ldquo; (Apostelgeschichte 1,3). Wie viel wei&szlig;t du &uuml;ber die Dinge des Reiches Gottes und wie gut lebst du das Leben im Reich Gottes?</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><b>GIB DEM REICH GOTTES VORRANG</b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In diesem Jahr wird buchst&auml;blich jeder Bedarf gedeckt werden. Tats&auml;chlich k&ouml;nnen wir uns die Sorgen sparen, wenn wir nur unsere Priorit&auml;ten richtig setzen. Und das ist eine Anweisung f&uuml;r diese Zeit und dar&uuml;ber hinaus. Dem Reich Gottes Priorit&auml;t einzur&auml;umen bedeutet, seinen Zweck, seine Mission, seine Werte, Ziele und Kultur &uuml;ber alles andere zu stellen. Wie Jesus versprochen hat: &bdquo;Trachtet zuerst nach dem Reich Gottes und nach seiner Gerechtigkeit, so wird euch alles andere zufallen&ldquo; (Matth&auml;us 6,33). Als Jesus &bdquo;alles andere&ldquo; sagte, meinte er die grundlegenden Bed&uuml;rfnisse des Lebens, Dinge, f&uuml;r die der Rest der Welt Tag und Nacht schuftet, um ein bequemes und angenehmes Leben zu f&uuml;hren. All das geh&ouml;rt uns und noch viel mehr in Christus Jesus, ganz besonders in diesem Jahr des Lebens im Reich Gottes, wenn wir das Reich Gottes &uuml;ber alles andere stellen.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><b>DIEN DEM ZWECK DES REICHES</b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Gott hat einen Plan f&uuml;r dein Leben; Gott hat einen Plan f&uuml;r sein Reich, mit dem auch dein Leben verbunden ist. Und in diesem Jahr des Lebens im Reich Gottes ruft Er dich dazu auf, dies mehr denn je zu erkennen und dich f&uuml;r die Absicht des Reiches einzusetzen. Du kannst ganz einfach f&uuml;r dich selbst oder f&uuml;r deine Familie leben. Aber es gibt einen besseren Weg zu leben und einen gr&ouml;&szlig;eren Sinn, f&uuml;r den es sich zu leben lohnt. Das ist, der Absicht des Reiches zu dienen. Wie Er alle Dinge zum Guten f&uuml;r diejenigen wirkt, die Ihn lieben und nach Seiner Absicht berufen sind (siehe R&ouml;mer 8,28). Es gibt viel zu diesem Thema zu sagen, aber dies ist nicht der richtige Ort daf&uuml;r. Wie Mordechai zu Esther sagte: &bdquo;Wer wei&szlig;, ob du nicht gerade f&uuml;r eine Zeit wie diese ins K&ouml;nigreich gekommen bist?&ldquo; (Esther 4,14). Genauso gibt es einen Zweck f&uuml;r dich, im K&ouml;nigreich zu dienen, und du solltest dich daf&uuml;r engagieren wie nie zuvor.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><b>VERBREITE DAS EVANGELIUM DES K&Ouml;NIGREICHS</b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Jesus hat mal gesagt: &bdquo;Dieses Evangelium vom Reich wird in der ganzen Welt verk&uuml;ndet werden, damit alle V&ouml;lker es h&ouml;ren; dann wird das Ende kommen&ldquo; (Matth&auml;us 24,14). Und das ist oberste Priorit&auml;t im Reich Gottes, allen Menschen &uuml;berall die gute Nachricht zu bringen. Und du hast dabei was zu tun. Mach mit, teile die gute Nachricht vom Reich Gottes mit den Menschen in deiner Umgebung, deinen Freunden, Nachbarn, Kollegen und allen, denen du begegnen und mit denen du &uuml;ber Jesus sprechen kannst. Erz&auml;hl ihnen vom K&ouml;nig, seiner Liebe zu ihnen, seiner Einladung an sie und dem Reich, das f&uuml;r sie vorbereitet ist. Lass sie wissen, dass Jesus der Weg ist. Eines Tages wird Gott jeden von uns f&uuml;r diejenigen zur Rechenschaft ziehen, die durch uns das Evangelium h&ouml;ren sollten. Du m&ouml;chtest doch dieser treue Diener sein, der den Willen des Vaters getan hat. Manchmal reicht es schon, jemanden zu einer Veranstaltung des Reiches einzuladen oder ihm eine kostenlose Ausgabe von &bdquo;Your Daily Light&ldquo; zu geben, die die Botschaft des Evangeliums vermittelt. Du kannst auch einfach den Link zur mobilen App weitergeben, damit sie sie herunterladen k&ouml;nnen. All das geh&ouml;rt dazu, das Evangelium zu verbreiten.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><b>INVESTIER IN DAS VORANBRINGEN DES REICHES</b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Als Teil der Prophezeiungen &uuml;ber Jesus verk&uuml;ndete der Prophet Jesaja: &bdquo;Die Vermehrung seines Reiches wird kein Ende haben&ldquo; (Jesaja 9,6). Gott hat den Plan, sein Reich voranzubringen und seine Herrschaft in allen Bereichen des Lebens zu etablieren. Er m&ouml;chte seine Herrschaft in jedem Land, in jeder Regierung, in jeder Institution und in jedem Leben etablieren. Dies ist nur durch die kontinuierliche Missionsarbeit m&ouml;glich, Menschen f&uuml;r den Herrn zu erreichen. Dies ist in vielerlei Hinsicht mit Kosten verbunden. Und Gott l&auml;dt uns ein, mehr Zeit und Ressourcen als je zuvor in die F&ouml;rderung des Reiches Gottes zu investieren, indem wir Dienste unterst&uuml;tzen und Dienern erm&ouml;glichen, in seinem Dienst effektiver zu sein. Und das ist die beste Rendite, die du jemals erzielen kannst, wenn du in die F&ouml;rderung des Reiches Gottes investierst.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Wie Jesus sagte: Sammelt euch keine Sch&auml;tze auf der Erde, wo Motten und Rost sie zerst&ouml;ren und Diebe einbrechen und stehlen. Er sagte: Sammelt euch Sch&auml;tze im Himmel, wo sie ewiglich sind. Mehr noch, er hat uns garantiert, dass wir alles, was wir f&uuml;r seine Zwecke in diesem Leben und im kommenden Leben, dem ewigen Leben, aufgeben, hundertfach zur&uuml;ckbekommen werden. Deshalb solltet ihr in diesem Jahr noch bewusster f&uuml;r die F&ouml;rderung des Reiches Gottes spenden. Es ist nicht die Zeit, sich zur&uuml;ckzulehnen, wenn ihr das bisher getan habt. Es ist Zeit, euer Engagement zu vervielfachen und noch opferbereiter zu geben (siehe Matth&auml;us 6,19-20 und Markus 10,29-30).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dies ist der Auftrag, den wir als Lighthouse Global Missions erf&uuml;llen, um Gottes Reich voranzubringen, genau wie viele andere Dienste. Wir nutzen viele Wege, um Menschen auf der ganzen Welt das Wort Gottes zu bringen. Durch Veranstaltungen, philanthropische Eins&auml;tze, die Ver&ouml;ffentlichung und Verteilung von aufschlussreichem Material in Buchform oder durch unsere weltweit zug&auml;ngliche mobile App. Wir bringen gro&szlig;e finanzielle Opfer, um dies zu erm&ouml;glichen. Auch du kannst dabei sein. Wenn du diesem Wort folgst, in die Ausbreitung des Reiches Gottes zu investieren, solltest du eine Partnerschaft mit Lighthouse Global Missions durch eine Spende in Betracht ziehen. Du wirst uns dabei helfen, die Wirkung unserer Mission zu verst&auml;rken.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In diesem Jahr des Lebens im Reich Gottes gibt es so viel zu entdecken und so viel zu wachsen, w&auml;hrend Gott seine Kraft und Herrlichkeit auf beispiellose Weise in unserem Leben offenbart. Als Teil deiner Verantwortung, dich auszurichten, solltest du die oben genannten f&uuml;nf Aspekte beachten. Begleite uns auch dieses Jahr wieder mit den Andachten von &bdquo;Your Daily Light&ldquo;. Durch deren Inhalte wirst du wertvolle Einblicke in das Leben im Reich Gottes gewinnen und es f&uuml;r dich selbst lebendig werden lassen.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Es ist mein Gebet, dass Gottes Gnade in deinem Leben reichlich vermehrt wird und dass er dich in allen Dingen gedeihen l&auml;sst, wie es f&uuml;r das Leben im Reich Gottes charakteristisch ist. In Jesu Namen.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Gott segne dich</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Mit der Liebe Gottes</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Schick mir eine pers&ouml;nliche E-Mail an PastorSimon@lgmissions.org</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">und teile mir dein Feedback und deine Zeugnisse mit. Du kannst mir auch mitteilen, wie ich f&uuml;r dich beten kann.</p>\r\n<p></p>', 'news', '0', '1', '2025-05-15', '2025-05-15'),
(30, '1756043084.JPG', 'LOOK TO JESUS', 'REGARDEZ VERS JÉSUS', 'SCHAU AUF JESUS', 'Simon T. Mungwa', '2024-08-25 01:44:40', '2025-08-24 01:50:54', 'admin@admin.com', 'admin@admin.com', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There has been a word on my heart for you this season, it is a call to look to Jesus in confident trust and faith, knowing this, that you will not be put to shame. You will not be disappointed by trusting in Him for whatever situation you have at hand or circumstances you are facing. Or maybe you are not dealing with any such challenging situations right now. It is still a word of assurance for you.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">How the Psalmist testified: <em><strong>&ldquo;Those who look to him for help will be radiant with joy; no shadow of shame will darken their faces&rdquo; (Psalm 34:5)</strong>.</em> It is a guaranteed word: No shadow of shame shall cover your face for trusting in the Lord.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Testimonies abound of people who resolutely set their hearts on the Lord and trusted Him in the most difficult situations. And in the end, they walked with their heads high up, because the Lord proved Himself to be their helper. We can easily think of Daniel thrown into the lions&rsquo; den. Or the three Hebrew men who were thrown into a furnace of fire (See Daniel 3:8-25, Daniel 6). All staged by those who opposed them, it only played out for their vindication and promotion. How this echoes in the words: <em>&ldquo;All things work together for good to those who love God, to those who are the called according to His purpose&rdquo; (See Romans 8:28).</em></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Even much so now, Jesus has become the object of our trust in God. Just as it is written, <em>&ldquo;See, I lay a stone in Zion, a chosen and precious cornerstone, and the one who trusts in him will never be put to shame&rdquo; (1 Peter 2:6).</em> That was God speaking to the prophet Isaiah, declaring things to come concerning Jesus (See Isaiah 28:16). Jesus is that precious cornerstone. And what an assurance, anyone who trusts in Him will never be put to shame. Look to Jesus, and He will cause all things to work for your good.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The author of Hebrews admonished: <em>&ldquo;<u>Looking away <strong>[from all that will distract]</strong> to Jesus</u>, who is the Leader and the Source of our faith [giving the first incentive for our belief] and is also its Finisher [bringing it to maturity and perfection].&rdquo; (Hebrews 12:2 Amplified).</em></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Maybe you have been looking at your finances and calculating your bank balance. It is time to look to Jesus. Maybe you received a medical report with bad prognosis. It is time to look to Jesus. Maybe you are dealing with some legal issues or administrative huddles. You could be looking to some open doors. Just whatever the situation or need is, it is time you looked to Jesus. Everything else is a distraction, seeking to take your attention away from Him who is worthy of it all.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once the children of Israel faced a situation with venomous snakes on their journey into that which God had promised them. As a remedy, God instructed Moses to make a bronze snake and put up on a pole. And whoever was bitten by a snake only had to look up to it and be saved (See Numbers 21:6-9). Even so Jesus compared himself to that bronze serpent. For He too was going to be raised up in crucifixion, so that whoever looks to Him shall be saved. Even today, Jesus is your way out of any challenging situation, if you will look to Him.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">He is Jesus, the beginning and the end, the author and the finisher. He has the keys of hell and of death. He is the head of all principalities, upholding all things by His powerful word. He opens a door, and no one can close. And His word concerning you is final. Look to Jesus today, who is able to save, deliver, heal, prosper, guide, defend, restore, and bless you.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I pray, that the Lord will cause you to see Jesus enthroned in your life and reigning over every situation, bringing you into the fullness of His great plans for your life. In Jesus&rsquo; name.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Grace be multiplied to you.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Email:</strong> PastorSimon@LGmissions.org</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For feedback, testimonies, prayer requests&nbsp;or partnership.</p>', '<p>&lt;C\'est un appel &agrave; regarder vers J&eacute;sus dans la confiance et la foi, sachant que vous n\'aurez pas &agrave; rougir. Vous ne serez pas d&eacute;&ccedil;us en vous confiant &agrave; lui, quelle que soit la situation que vous avez ou les circonstances auxquelles vous &ecirc;tes confront&eacute;s. Ou peut-&ecirc;tre n\'&ecirc;tes-vous pas confront&eacute; &agrave; de telles situations difficiles en ce moment. C\'est toujours une parole d\'assurance pour vous.</p>\r\n<p>Comme en t&eacute;moigne le Psalmiste : <em><strong>&ldquo;Ceux qui se tournent vers lui pour obtenir du secours seront rayonnants de joie ; aucune ombre de honte n\'obscurcira leur visage&amp;rdquo ; (Psaume 34:5)</strong>.</em> C\'est une parole garantie : Aucune ombre de honte ne couvrira votre visage pour avoir fait confiance au Seigneur.</p>\r\n<p>Les t&eacute;moignages abondent sur ce sujet.</p>\r\n<p>De m&ecirc;me, aujourd\'hui, il n\'y a pas de doute que l\'on ne peut pas faire l\'&eacute;conomie d\'une r&eacute;flexion sur l\'avenir de l\'humanit&eacute;.</p>\r\n<p>Aujourd\'hui encore, J&eacute;sus est devenu l\'objet de notre confiance en Dieu. Comme il est &eacute;crit, <em>&ldquo;Voici, je pose une pierre en Sion, une pierre d\'angle choisie et pr&eacute;cieuse, et celui qui se confie en elle ne sera jamais confondu&amp;rdquo ; (1 Pierre 2:6).</em> C\'&eacute;tait Dieu qui parlait au proph&egrave;te Isa&iuml;e, d&eacute;clarant les choses &agrave; venir concernant J&eacute;sus (Voir Isa&iuml;e 28:16). J&eacute;sus est cette pr&eacute;cieuse pierre angulaire. Et quelle assurance, quiconque se confie en lui ne sera jamais couvert de honte. Regardez &agrave; J&eacute;sus, et il fera concourir toutes choses &agrave; votre bien.</p>\r\n<p>L\'auteur de l\'&eacute;p&icirc;tre aux H&eacute;breux a mis en garde : <em>&ldquo;<u>Les regards se d&eacute;tournent <strong>[de tout ce qui distrait]</strong> vers J&eacute;sus</u>, qui est le Chef et la Source de notre foi [donnant le premier encouragement &agrave; notre croyance] et qui est aussi son Finisseur [l\'amenant &agrave; la maturit&eacute; et &agrave; la perfection].&amp;rdquo ; (H&eacute;breux 12:2 Amplifi&eacute;).</em></p>\r\n<p>Peut-&ecirc;tre que vous n\'avez jamais eu l\'occasion de vous confier &agrave; J&eacute;sus, et qu\'il fera en sorte que toutes les choses concourent &agrave; votre bien.</p>\r\n<p>Peut-&ecirc;tre avez-vous regard&eacute; vos finances et calcul&eacute; votre solde bancaire. Il est temps de regarder vers J&eacute;sus. Peut-&ecirc;tre avez-vous re&ccedil;u un rapport m&eacute;dical avec un mauvais pronostic. Il est temps de vous tourner vers J&eacute;sus. Vous &ecirc;tes peut-&ecirc;tre confront&eacute; &agrave; des questions juridiques ou &agrave; des probl&egrave;mes administratifs. Vous pourriez chercher des portes ouvertes. Quelle que soit la situation ou le besoin, il est temps de regarder vers J&eacute;sus. Tout le reste n\'est que distraction, cherchant &agrave; d&eacute;tourner votre attention de Celui qui est digne de tout cela.</p>\r\n<p>La gr&acirc;ce soit multipli&eacute;e pour vous.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><strong>Email:</strong> PastorSimon@LGmissions.org</p>\r\n<p>Pour des commentaires, des t&eacute;moignages, des demandes de pri&egrave;res&nbsp;ou un partenariat.</p>', '<p>Es gibt ein Wort, das mir in dieser Jahreszeit auf dem Herzen liegt. Es ist ein Aufruf, in zuversichtlichem Vertrauen und Glauben auf Jesus zu schauen, in dem Wissen, dass ihr nicht zuschanden werden werdet. Ihr werdet nicht entt&auml;uscht werden, wenn ihr auf ihn vertraut, egal in welcher Situation oder unter welchen Umst&auml;nden ihr euch gerade befindet. Vielleicht haben Sie aber auch gerade keine derart herausfordernden Situationen vor sich. Es ist trotzdem ein Wort der Zuversicht f&uuml;r Sie.</p>\r\n<p>&gt;</p>\r\n<p>Wie der Psalmist bezeugt: <em><strong>&ldquo;Diejenigen, die auf ihn um Hilfe schauen, werden vor Freude strahlen; kein Schatten der Schande wird ihr Angesicht verdunkeln&rdquo; (Psalm 34:5)</strong>.</em> Es ist ein verb&uuml;rgtes Wort: Kein Schatten der Schande wird dein Gesicht bedecken, weil du auf den Herrn vertraust.</p>\r\n<p>Es gibt viele Zeugnisse von Menschen, die ihr Herz entschlossen auf den Herrn setzten und ihm in den schwierigsten Situationen vertrauten. Und am Ende sind sie erhobenen Hauptes gegangen, weil der Herr sich als ihr Helfer erwiesen hat. Wir k&ouml;nnen leicht an Daniel denken, der in die L&ouml;wengrube geworfen wurde. Oder an die drei hebr&auml;ischen M&auml;nner, die in einen Feuerofen geworfen wurden (siehe Daniel 3:8-25, Daniel 6). Alle wurden von ihren Gegnern inszeniert und dienten nur ihrer Rechtfertigung und Bef&ouml;rderung. Wie das in den Worten widerhallt: &ldquo;Alles wirkt zum Guten f&uuml;r die, die Gott lieben, f&uuml;r die, die nach seinem Vorsatz berufen sind&rdquo; (siehe R&ouml;mer 8,28).</p>\r\n<p>Jetzt erst recht ist Jesus zum Gegenstand unseres Gottvertrauens geworden. So wie es geschrieben steht: <em>&ldquo;Siehe, ich lege in Zion einen Stein, einen auserw&auml;hlten und kostbaren Eckstein, und wer auf ihn vertraut, der wird nicht zuschanden werden&rdquo; (1 Petrus 2:6).</em> Das war Gott, der zum Propheten Jesaja sprach und die kommenden Dinge &uuml;ber Jesus verk&uuml;ndete (siehe Jesaja 28:16). Jesus ist dieser kostbare Eckstein. Und was f&uuml;r eine Zusicherung: Wer auf ihn vertraut, wird niemals zuschanden werden. Schauen Sie auf Jesus, und er wird alles zu Ihrem Besten machen.</p>\r\n<p>&gt;</p>\r\n<p>Der Autor des Hebr&auml;erbriefs mahnt: <em>&ldquo;<u>Seht weg <strong>[von allem, was euch ablenken wird]</strong> zu Jesus</u>, der der Leiter und die Quelle unseres Glaubens ist [der den ersten Ansporn f&uuml;r unseren Glauben gibt] und auch sein Vollender [der ihn zur Reife und Vollkommenheit bringt].&rdquo; (Hebr&auml;er 12:2 Amplified).</em></p>\r\n<p>Vielleicht haben Sie auf Ihre Finanzen geschaut und Ihren Kontostand berechnet. Es ist an der Zeit, auf Jesus zu schauen. Vielleicht haben Sie einen medizinischen Bericht mit einer schlechten Prognose erhalten. Es ist an der Zeit, auf Jesus zu schauen. Vielleicht haben Sie mit rechtlichen Fragen oder administrativen Problemen zu k&auml;mpfen. Sie k&ouml;nnten nach offenen T&uuml;ren Ausschau halten. Was auch immer die Situation oder das Bed&uuml;rfnis ist, es ist an der Zeit, dass Sie auf Jesus schauen. Alles andere ist eine Ablenkung, die Ihre Aufmerksamkeit von dem ablenken soll, der all das wert ist.</p>\r\n<p>&gt;</p>\r\n<p>Einmal sahen sich die Kinder Israels auf ihrer Reise in das Land, das Gott ihnen versprochen hatte, mit giftigen Schlangen konfrontiert. Gott wies Mose an, eine bronzene Schlange anzufertigen und sie an einem Pfahl aufzuh&auml;ngen. Und wer von einer Schlange gebissen wurde, brauchte nur zu ihr aufzublicken, um gerettet zu werden (siehe Numeri 21,6-9). So verglich sich auch Jesus mit dieser bronzenen Schlange. Denn auch er sollte durch die Kreuzigung auferweckt werden, so dass jeder, der auf ihn schaut, gerettet wird. Auch heute ist Jesus dein Ausweg aus jeder schwierigen Situation, wenn du auf ihn blickst.</p>\r\n<p>&gt;</p>\r\n<p>Er ist Jesus, der Anfang und das Ende, der Urheber und der Vollender. Er hat die Schl&uuml;ssel der H&ouml;lle und des Todes. Er ist das Haupt aller F&uuml;rstent&uuml;mer und h&auml;lt alle Dinge durch sein m&auml;chtiges Wort aufrecht. Er &ouml;ffnet eine T&uuml;r, und niemand kann sie schlie&szlig;en. Und sein Wort &uuml;ber Sie ist endg&uuml;ltig. Schauen Sie heute auf Jesus, der in der Lage ist, Sie zu retten, zu befreien, zu heilen, zu f&ouml;rdern, zu leiten, zu verteidigen, wiederherzustellen und zu segnen.</p>\r\n<p>Ich bete, dass der Herr Sie dazu bringt, Jesus in Ihrem Leben thronen zu sehen und &uuml;ber jede Situation zu herrschen und Sie in die F&uuml;lle seiner gro&szlig;en Pl&auml;ne f&uuml;r Ihr Leben zu bringen. In Jesus&rsquo; Namen.</p>\r\n<p>Gnade sei mit Ihnen vervielfacht.</p>\r\n<p>Simon T. Mungwa</p>\r\n<p><strong>Email:</strong> PastorSimon@LGmissions.org</p>\r\n<p>F&uuml;r Feedback, Zeugnisse, Gebetsanliegen oder Partnerschaft.</p>', 'news', '0', '1', '2025-08-24', '2025-08-24');
